@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ Range window (plan §2 #103–#106): a third root, `RangeApp.vue` over `rangeSto
 
 Folder sums (plan §2 #125): `rangeFolderSums.ts` `folderSums` (once per file list in `RangeApp.vue`) keys each folder's `+a −r` by the path its tree row carries; `RangeApp.vue` fills the tree's optional `folder` slot (`FileTree.vue`, forwarded by `FileList.vue`; the merge window passes none) with `RangeCounts.vue`, the one `+a −r` pair `RangeFileRow.vue` uses too.
 
+Collapse toggle (plan §2 #126): `RangeView.vue`'s header button after Previous/Next reads and writes the merge window's stored choice through `createCollapsing` in the range store; its words are `collapsing.ts` `COLLAPSE_LABEL`, which the merge toolbar's `LABELS` uses too.
+
 Range threads (plan §2 #116–#120): `rangeThreads.ts` (list, open set, drafts through `rangeDrafts.ts`, counts, `boxOf`) and `rangeGitLab.ts` (the check, Send, `postButton`/`sendButton`, the send result) are held by `rangeStore`; every thread word is in `rangeThreadText.ts` (labels, prompts, `threadCountText`, `sendNoticeRow`; Copy/Copied are `serverText.ts`'s). `RangeView` renders `RangeThreadLayer.vue`, which teleports one `RangeThreadBox.vue` per key of `useRangeController`'s `threadHosts` into the host the editor keeps for that thread, so a box keeps its DOM, focus and typed text across CodeMirror redraws. A box is a draft (place, text, Comment/Cancel) or an open thread (place, collapse, one `RangeMessage.vue` per message, the reply field); a collapsed thread has no host and so no box. `RangeMessage` shows a note's text or the one `aiAnswer` line (an exhaustive switch C replaces), or in its place the message's open `RangeMessageEditor.vue`; the `postButton` (disabled ones keep their sentence as title on a wrapper), the posting label, and for a pending message the link as selectable text with Copy (a failed clipboard write selects the link). `postButton` returns the label, the title and the press action (`write` | `unqueue` | null); `write` opens `RangeMessageEditor.vue` (`box="post"`, label "Text to post", Queue) in the message's place by writing a `post` draft (`rangeDrafts.ts`, keyed by `MessageId`: `postDraft`/`writePost`/`dropPost`), so a half-edited Post text survives a collapse and the 16-view eviction; a queue that lands drops it, and focus moves to the message's Post/Unqueue button after a queue or a Cancel. `RangeMessageEditor.vue` is the one in-place message editor for Post and Edit: it reads and writes the draft its `box` names, focuses its field on mount, keeps its submit off while the text is blank or `offTitle` is set (shown as the title), keeps focus in the field on a submit press (`@mousedown.prevent`) and emits `submit`/`cancel`. A failed clipboard write selects the link (`copyOrSelect.ts`, shared with `ServerMenu`). Keys in every box field go through `rangeKeys.ts` `boxKeydown`: `Mod-Enter` submits and `Escape` cancels (built with `keys.ts` `keyList`, matched by `pressesKey`; only the composing check is its own) (a draft is dropped, a reply cleared), both `preventDefault` and `stopPropagation`; every other key stays the field's. `RangeApp` calls `fileListKey(event, navigator.platform)` as the other roots do; the reply's Comment keeps focus in the reply field (`@mousedown.prevent`). `RangeSendButton.vue` sits left of the gear in each `RangeView` header; `RangeApp` shows the last send's result (`sendNoticeRow`) as a closable `NoticeBar` row and passes each file's thread count to `RangeFileRow` (a muted speech bubble, none at 0).
 
 Edit and Delete (plan §2 #123): `rangeNoteChange.ts` holds both rules — `isChangeable` (a note not pending) decides whether `RangeMessage.vue` shows them, and `noteChangeBlock(sending, aiTurn)` (a send running first, then the thread's AI turn) turns them and Save off, with `noteChangeTitle`'s hover text. Edit writes an `edit` draft (`rangeDrafts.ts` `editDraft`/`writeEdit`/`dropEdit`), shown in the message's place by `RangeMessageEditor.vue` (`box="edit"`, label "Comment text", Save; its `offTitle` is the block's title); writing an `edit` draft drops the message's `post` draft and the reverse, so the two boxes are never open at once. `editNote` sends only a non-blank text and drops the draft when stored; focus returns to Edit after Save or Cancel. Delete goes through `rangeStore`'s `deleteNote`, which asks `{ kind: "deleteNote" }` first. Every list a reply brings (`setList`) drops the open state and the reply, Post and Edit drafts of threads and messages it no longer holds, and the Edit draft of a note no longer changeable (a Send that made it pending closes its box), so a thread removed with its last note leaves nothing behind.
